s=s[:start]+'''<pre>G_c(h) = sum over observed intervals ending by h:
           gamma(elapsed) * measured_dt * N_c(actual_channel_c)
         + gamma(d) * V_target_c(last_state,g,h-d)  [eligible cuts only]
V_c(S,g,0) = 0
value_loss = mean over valid channels of (V_c(start_state,g,h) - G_c(h))^2</pre>
<p>Use h of 0.5, 1, 2 or 3 seconds. A complete target is an actual contiguous window of exactly that duration under the same retained intention and behavior policy; it has no added tail. During warm-up use only those complete windows. Later, a cut after d seconds may use a fixed target-head estimate for h-d only if that remaining duration, channel and policy already have a held-out error bound. Otherwise save the partial record without making that value target. Never treat a three-second window ending as the end of all future usefulness, or bootstrap an unspecified infinite return.</p>
<p>The head concatenates core state, normalized body/object/contact fields, validity masks, intention descriptor and remaining duration h. Two 256-unit GELU layers output one value per active channel and a separate accumulated goal-potential output. Its target copy updates only after an accepted finite optimizer update: <code>target = 0.995*target + 0.005*current</code>. Stop gradients through that target while calculating the loss. The three-second continuation used by the planner is taught from actual three-second windows beginning in the relevant states; it never counts the explicit preceding three seconds again.</p>
<p>Only windows in which that same intention g was actually retained and the specified behavior policy ran can teach this goal-conditioned value. Exploration without a pursued g supplies forward lessons and retrieval examples, not invented goal-conditioned targets. Pin the behavior policy, representation, raw-channel normalization and weight version. A changed chooser starts a new value epoch. Preserve unfinished old-epoch windows under their old version; complete them only from matching old-version evidence, otherwise retain them as partial evidence without a new-epoch value lesson. Re-encode raw windows after an encoder change, or retain their old representation; never mix incompatible features.</p>
<p>While continuation is unqualified, use zero continuation and the qualified three-second forecast plus explicit goal-distance heuristic. Label that shorter comparison in the decision record. It can collect actual intention-bearing windows inside the qualified physical envelope. Goal acquisition from exploration is allowed only when the short-horizon raw utility forecasts qualify; otherwise exploration continues. No earlier exploratory endpoint is relabelled as the intention that supposedly caused it.</p>
<p>A true completed physical episode has no tail. A pause preserves the pending window, intention and elapsed simulated time. A time-limit cut follows the remaining-duration rule above and never crosses a reset. A physical fault records actual harm and ends that episode. If a support shift is followed by measured control benefit within the observed window, that benefit enters the earlier state's G target. This is how a later result changes an earlier value estimate. Benefits beyond the declared six-second comparison remain outside this initial chooser until a longer horizon is qualified.</p>
''' +s[end:]
